## Overview

Take-Two describes Grand Theft Auto VI as a single-player experience.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}}

## Premise

The official site follows protagonists Jason and Lucia in Vice City, USA, who are drawn into a criminal conspiracy that reaches across the state of Leonida after a job goes wrong.{{cite:gta6-official-site}}

## Platform and technical features

Sony's PlayStation listing highlights several PS5-specific presentation and control features, including Tempest 3D Audio, use of the console's high-speed SSD to shorten loading times, haptic feedback, adaptive triggers, and the DualSense built-in speaker.{{cite:playstation-gta6}} The same listing says PlayStation 4 hardware cannot run the title.{{cite:playstation-gta6}}

Digital purchases on PlayStation 5 can be downloaded to the primary console tied to an account, using that system's sharing-and-offline-play option, and can also be used on other PS5 consoles when the buyer signs in.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}}

Microsoft said the game would be playable at launch through Xbox Cloud Gaming for Xbox One as well as Series X and Series S, with streaming beginning at 1 a.m. ET on November 19.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}} Series X and Series S owners can play a native version and may pre-install it; when the title is streamed, it uses Series S graphics settings.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}} Starting November 11, players in supported markets could purchase streaming hours for eligible titles even if they do not subscribe to Game Pass, and Microsoft notes that availability, devices, and eligibility vary by market.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}} Microsoft also states that the game has to be bought separately for cloud play.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

## Editions and in-game bonuses

Rockstar and Take-Two describe an Ultimate Edition that bundles exclusive vehicles, weapons, apparel, and chapter-linked bonuses for Jason and Lucia across their story.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}} Store listings name specific bonus items, including the Shitzu Squalo watercraft and a '67 Vapid Dominator Buggy that can be stored at the Paradise Garage.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}}{{cite:taketwo-preorders}} Some of those descriptions say the Paradise Garage includes a weapon locker and a secure place to leave stolen goods for fencing.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}}{{cite:gta6-official-site}}

